                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "If you're keen for a punnet square game and this is on sale, then by all means go ahead, it's not a bad game at all and it does teach that basic first step of genetics. I don't regret picking it up as a casual cosy game and my kids will probably get a few hours joy from it too. The magical plants are cute and the reasons customers want them are amusing.\n\nI just wouldn't particularly recommend it because it's very short (finished in 3 hours) and simple, no further concepts like codominance or incomplete dominance are covered, so it gets a bit repetitive towards the end. Something like Niche takes the genetics concept and does it better in my opinion. Oddly, if you make a silly mistake or buy an inefficient thing in the first couple of days then it's not very forgiving (only buy power upgrades at first, close the shop when you run out of breeding power). The voices remind me a bit of the old Microsoft Sam, probably because the game is now over a decade old, though the characters really aren't the point of the game so I don't find that a problem.",
